[2024-11-08Major MapMajor Map for the Department of Economics, National Chengchi University

PhD: A total of 38 credits


	Required Elective (4 credits)


		Seminar on Economic Problems (must be taken for at least 4 semesters)



	Required (24 credits)

	1st year


		Microeconomic Theory (I)(II) (3 credits each)
		Macroeconomic Theory (I)(II) (3 credits each)
		Econometrics (I)(II) (3 credits each)


	2nd year


		Advanced Microeconomics Analysis (3 credits)
		Advanced Macroeconomics Analysis (3 credits)



	Elective (10 credits)


		Students may select up to 10 credits from courses outside the department. However, to ensure alignment with professional and academic goals, it is recommended that electives be primarily chosen from the doctoral program offered by this department. Consultation with academic advisors and thesis supervisors is advised when opting for courses from other departments.



	Degree Conferral

	Completion of Required Courses and Credits

	Completion of the Subject Examination


		Subjects：Two foundational subjects (Microeconomic Theory, Macroeconomic Theory) and one specialized subject.
		Examination Attempts：Students must pass the doundational subject exa,s within five semesters of enrollment. If a student fails the same foundational subject exam three times or does not pass the specialized subject exam within seven semesters, they will be dismissed from the program. The specified time limits include any period of leave.For more details, please look at the "Qualification Assessment Guidelines for Doctoral Candidates of the Department of Economics, National Chengchi University (Applicable to students addmitted from the 2021 academic year onwards)".


	Academic Research Ethics Education Course

	Completion of the Degree Examination


		Students must have at least 10 points from paper presentations to apply for the thesis oral defense.



