PhD: A total of 32 credits


	Required Elective (4 credits)


		Seminar on Economic Problems (must be taken for at least 4 semesters)



	Required (15 credits)

	1st year


		Microeconomic Theory (III)(IV) (3 credits each)
		Macroeconomic Theory (III)(IV) (3 credits each)
		Econometrics (II) (3 credits)



	Elective (13 credits)


		Students may choose up to 9 credits from courses outside the department,but the credits will only be recognized after approval from the department chair, advisor, or thesis supervisor.



	Degree Conferral

	Completion of Required Courses and Credits

	Completion of the Subject Examination


		Subjects：Two foundational subjects (Microeconomic Theory, Macroeconomic Theory) and one specialized subject (students must complete the related courses (III) or (IV) before being eligible to take the exam).
		Examination Attempts：Students may take the same foundational subject exam up to three times. The specialized subject exam must be passed within seven semesters. Failure to meet these requirements will result in dismissal from the program.


	Academic Research Ethics Education Course

	Completion of the Degree Examination


		Students must have at least 10 points from paper presentations to apply for the thesis oral defense.



